**Adjusting server configuration**

I realized that the correct pattern for SPA under the subpath should look like this: 

```
location /admin/ {
    root /var/www/etl-tst.chococraft.ru;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /admin/index.html;
}
```

However, since the file `admin/index.html` does not exist, I'll need to use ‘alias’ instead. I'll set it up with: 

```
location /admin/ { auth; alias /var/www/etl-tst.chococraft.ru/; try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html; }
```

The previous setup caused errors due to the way it redirected internally.

**Updating server configuration**

The right setup for the /admin location involves using:

```
location /admin/ {
    auth_basic ...;
    root /var/www/etl-tst.chococraft.ru;
    index index.html;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /admin/index.html;
}
```

But, since `/admin/index.html` does not exist, I need to use 'alias' for proper mapping. So I’ll change it to:

```
location /admin/ {
    alias /var/www/etl-tst.chococraft.ru/;
    index index.html;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
}
```

With 'alias', the URI part follows correctly. I'll make these changes and reload the configuration.

